WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.828
Speak audibly at an appropriate pace, pause at punctuation and pronounce words

00:00:04.828 --> 00:00:05.213
clearly.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:10.829
What is the purpose of a full stop during oral reading? Answer: Pause and mark the

00:00:10.829 --> 00:00:12.028
end of a sentence.

00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:17.304
Record or present a short announcement with natural pauses and correct stress.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.826
Discuss why: Pausing marks the sentence ending.
